# Environment Variables Setup

This file should contain your API keys for the NHS Tracker application.

## Required Variables

```env
# Google Vision API Key - Used for image verification (reverse image search, safety checks)
VITE_GOOGLE_VISION_API_KEY=your_google_vision_api_key_here

# Google Gemini API Key - Used for AI analysis of volunteer proof images
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Hack Club proxy API key (used for text-only verification)
VITE_HACKCLUB_API_KEY=your_hackclub_api_key_here

# Google Sheets API key - reads the leaderboard
VITE_GOOGLE_SHEETS_API_KEY=your_google_sheets_api_key_here

# The ID from your sheet URL: docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS PART>/edit
VITE_SPREADSHEET_ID=your_spreadsheet_id_here

# Apps Script web app URL that writes submissions (ends in /exec)
VITE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/your_script_id_here/exec

# Code that lets an officer skip AI image verification
VITE_ADMIN_OVERRIDE_CODE=your_admin_code_here
```

## Setup Instructions

1. Create a `.env` file in the `project/` directory
2. Copy the variables above and replace the values with your actual API keys
3. Never commit the `.env` file to version control (it's already in `.gitignore`)

## Getting API Keys

### Google Vision API
1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/)
2. Enable the Vision API
3. Create API credentials

### Google Gemini API
1. Go to [Google AI Studio](https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey)
2. Generate an API key

## Security Note

⚠️ **IMPORTANT**: Never share your API keys or commit them to version control. The `.env` file is already excluded in `.gitignore`.
